{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And as for me.</b> Lest you say that when the blessed El said to me, <b>and I will make you a congregation of peoples</b>, the intent was that I would beget more sons, but sin prevented this — this is impossible." "For <b>when I came from Paddan.</b> When the blessed El revealed Himself to me then." "<b>Rachel died upon me.</b> As they said, of blessed memory (Sanhedrin 22a): a woman dies only for her husband." "<b>On the road, while there was still a stretch of land to come to Ephrath.</b> Immediately upon departing from that place where the word of the blessed El had come to me, while I was still on the road before reaching Bethlehem, <b>and I buried her there on the road to Ephrat</b>. And so greatly did my anguish and mourning overpower me that I did not have strength to bring her to the burial grounds of Bethlehem, and there is no doubt that from then on my heart was hollow within me and the evil impulse no longer ruled over me, and my desire was weakened and no strength remained in me to beget sons."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:06.017453917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}